A||X||90||Smokin' GT||Killed a 2000 V6 mustang.... twice!||||7||
Z||000000||Smokin' GT||10-13-2001||04:54 AM||||So, I have a friend and we were hanging out at a party and he had this preconcieved notion that my car is slow, he advised me earlier not to get a fiero, but as we can see I did of course!  He drives a 2000/2001 V6 mustang (not sure exactly what year) with intake.  I personally thought it was kind of cool, well that was of course when i was driving a toyota wagon, and when I got the fiero, my world changed quite a bit.  So, I drive a basically stock 87 GT, the only mods so far are 180 degree thermostat and AC Delco rapid fire plugs, the car's got 160,000 on it but the engine is definitely rebuilt and once again partially rebuilt by me, so it's probably got less than 60,000 on it.  So after many snide remarks about how he was going to smoke me I got him to race me.  We went and got a flagger and found our nearby "drag road."  So the first time, I popped it and so did he but the limited slip jammed right in there and I literally flew a car length ahead, and we were the same distance away the rest of the race, he couldn't catch up.  He demanded a rematch of course, not believing that it was possible.  The next time I totally missed second, I had to practically jam it in, so he gained on me but still at the end he couldn't catch my nose, I beat him fair and square both times, stock.  So I'd love to see what would happen to BlackStang95 racing a fiero!  V6 Mustang? Camaro?  Bring it on! (I put to shame another friends '92 v6 camaro with exhaust, and have yet to race my friend with a '97 V6 Camaro with exhaust!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||7
Z||000001||GTMike||10-13-2001||09:21 AM||||way to go.  <P>i havn't been in a good race in so long.    a dakota rt was messing with me  last week but there was a bunch of trafic and i was turning at the next light.    i'm on the look out for him though||||reg||1
