Z||000024||Tryxalon||10-13-2001||08:38 PM||||2002 Mustang v-6 weighs at least 3066 pounds and engine produces 190 horses. 16/1 power/weight ratio<P>87 Fiero GT weights at least 2600 and engine produces at least 140 horse. about 17/1 power/weight ratio.  <P>That is really close, as far as comparing cars goes, and who wins on whatever day is based on driver/tune of car/ambient conditions or any of the other variables involved, more than a specific difference between the two vehicles.   <P>So what?  So a thumbs up "nice kill" Smoking' GT (it obviously has some meaning to him)  and a shrug cause it really doesn't matter to me!<BR>(except I think Ford stands for "Fix or Repair Daily") <P>Car races are kind of like horse races: proof that there is always more than one opinion on any subject! <P>   <p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
