Z||000051||Leadfoot||10-15-2001||10:32 AM||||Smokin'   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smokin_2.gif">   GT way to go!  When I first bought my fiero my friends showed it no mercy.  However, after I took each one of them for a ride they soon started looking at the fiero with a new respect.  I have raced a couple v6 cameros and mustangs and won each race by a large margin....well if you want to call it racing. I am usually not looking for a race but when you have guys like blackstang95 revving their engine at you with a "my v6 is stronger than your weak v6 grin" how can one resist.  My most memorable v6 stang kill was against this wanna be "player".  The stang was pimped out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pimp_2.gif">    rims, Borla exhaust, wing....I think you get the picture.  Anyway, he pulls along side me with the radio blasting.  At first I thought no one was in the car because he was sitting so low.  While we were waiting for the green he kept hammering the throttle so I turned my head at him and with a simple not of my head I graciously excepted his challenge.  When the light turned green I launched about a car length ahead and he never caught up.  After about a couple of blocks he fell back and never came back to the front of the line.  So I guess from the looks of it you and me must have limited edition fieros because they can beat V6 stangs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.ukobservers.net/cwm/otn/party/beerchug.gif">     <p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
