Z||000065||Voytek||10-16-2001||04:59 PM||||Thanks for resurrecting this thread guys!  Now I can add fuel to this thread.<P>Ok.  My '87 Fiero GT has the original engine, bored and stroked to a 3.1, perf. manifolds and no cat.  Those aren't totally serious mods but they're enough to do this:<P>I have recently KILLED a brand-spanking-new mustang V6 convertible (at least I asssume it was a V6.  I mean a V8 would just be a total embarrasment).  First, we came to a sharp corner, he behind, I in front.  So he gets on my a$$ to let me know that I'm slowing him down.  First, I thought 'let's see how well your 'stang can take this corner'.  After putting an additional 2 car lengths between us, we get to a 3 lane road.  He changes the lanes immediately, as if he's going to pass me, and floors it.  This is where the fun begun.  By the time we hit 130 kph (about 81 mph) he was about 5-6 car lengths behind me.  By the time we hit 160 kph (100 mph) he gave up.  For those locals who know Calgary, this was on Memorial, coming out of downtown.  I couldn't help but laugh.<P>Another quick story.  I raced 2, not 1 but 2, new 4.6 V8's (on separate occasions).  I was dead even with one guy and I was about 1/2-1 car length ahead of the other guy.  If done properly, the torque-to-weight ratio can really lauch the Fiero off the line.<P>Not to be too cocky, I was WHIPPED very badly by a late '80's 5.0 LX (they're a bit lighter than the GT).  Must have been pretty modified - the guy was just looking for a race.  I didn't try a second time.<P>Stock Mustang V6? Sorry but I won't waste my car on one of those again - too easy.<p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000066||Gerald||10-16-2001||05:38 PM||||I wasn't gonna post on this but the temptation got to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So anyway. I drive a 4 cyl fiero and yes I think its fast. But if I beat a 4 cyl stang I wouldn't brag too much. After all it was a 4 cyl. If I had a 6 cyl fiero I wouldn't brag about beating a 6 cyl stang. There is a definite weight issue here. I'm sure you can understand. What we need here is some cold hard numbers. I don't have them but I'm sure someone that's at least a little unbiased can find them. By the way cliff. You rock!!!!! Bunnys rule  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
