Z||000079||Formula||10-17-2001||09:20 AM||||I'm fairly sure the V6 stang weighs more around 3077 lbs. And a fiero weighs around 2800.<P>3077-2800= 277 lbs...<P>Every 100 lbs is the equilvalent of 10 hp..<P>so the mustang has to pull an extra 277 pounds which is the same as dropping the hp by 27.7.<P>Your car has a 150 hp, therefore running against a fiero it would act like it has 122.3 hp to the fieros 135.<P>A new stang would act like it has 162.3 hp compared to the fieros 135. but the Mustang still can't get traction on stop light runs.<P>also, you have to admit that the fiero has a lot better gear ratios then the mustang.<P>against a new V6:<BR>odds are, the fiero would win 0-30 then the mustang would win top end, but the qtr mile times would be almost identical. ~15.4<P>against an old V6:<BR>If the old V6 had a REALLY good driver it might be able to only get pulled by 1/2 or 1 car to 60mph lol.<P>think about it,<BR>your mustang: 3077 lbs 150 hp<BR>85 fiero gt: 2800 lbs 140 hp<P>your 10 horsepower isnt going to make up the extra 277 lbs.  How do you get your engine is so much better then ours, you have an extra liter making a whopping 10 more hp.  the (99+) new ones are fairly consistent with Fieros though.........<P>And btw, you dont have a new one, so you cant claim to have 190 hp.<P>*all stats are from <A HREF="http://www.kbb.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kbb.com</A>  for the mustang, and the fiero ones are off the top of my head*<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
